# Follow the skill as written

The skill file, and the reference files it tells you to open, are the whole task. Do what they say. Stop there.

## Do not add anything of your own

If the skill does not name it, do not add it. This includes a component, attribute, section, sentence, link, file, screenshot, or step.

Do not fill a gap from memory, from a framework default, or from another article, unless the skill says to copy that pattern.

If an addition looks useful and the skill is silent, stop and ask. Do not add it and explain afterwards.

## Examples

```
Wrong: <Card title="Activate protection" icon="toggle-on">
Right: <Card title="Activate protection" href="/ddos-protection/onboarding-service/service-activation">
```

The landing skill does not mention `icon`. The CDN and Account settings landings do not use it. Adding it is not part of the task.

```
Wrong: a sentence, card, or file the approved scheme and the skill do not list, added because it seems helpful.
Right: write only the scheme the skill and the user approved, then stop.
```
